IMPORT policy

-- Nine benchmark queries (Kant et al. 2025, Appendix A.2), applied to
-- `covered` from policy.l4. Standing preamble for every query: assume all
-- conditions not mentioned by the query are met and no exclusion not
-- mentioned is triggered; the agreement has been signed and the premium
-- has been paid on time.
--
-- Common "favorable, unrelated" defaults used below unless a query's own
-- facts say otherwise: agreement signed; premium paid at month 0; no
-- fraud/misrepresentation; wellness visit at month 1 with a qualified
-- provider; written confirmation at month 1; no dispute (so the
-- arbitration fields are moot); written proof of claim at month 0 with no
-- recovery yet sought (so the 60-day bar is moot); a 12-month policy
-- term.

-- Q1. will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while
-- doing my duty as a firefighter?
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                  IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`             IS 3
    `hospitalization ground`            IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`            IS 40
    `causes`                            IS LIST Firefighting
    `fraud month`                       IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`           IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`              IS JUST 1
    `wellness visit provider qualified` IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`        IS JUST 1
    `dispute arisen`                    IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`            IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`       IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`    IS TRUE
    `written proof of claim month`      IS JUST 0
    `recovery sought month`             IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                IS 12

#EVAL covered q1

